//! Duplicate-path pruning automaton, generated by `fsm.py 12`.
//!
//! A blank path is pruned when it ends in a string that a shorter or
//! lexicographically smaller path duplicates (identities up to 12
//! moves, 8081 states). A node is packed as `state << 4 | mask`,
//! where bit `d` of `mask` is set when moving the blank in slidy direction
//! `d` is allowed, so the move table can be indexed by the mask directly.

/// The packed start node: the start state, every direction allowed.
pub const START: u32 = 134159;

